+# Todo Due Dates Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [x]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Add optional calendar due dates and overdue filtering to the API and todo list for ticket #1.
+
+**Architecture:** Keep the singleton TodoStore as the common source for the API and Blazor page. Store dates as DateOnly values and compute overdue status from the UTC calendar day when read. Keep request dates as strings so TodoStore can validate them using ValidationException; distinguish omitted PATCH dates from explicit null with an init-property presence flag.
+
+**Tech Stack:** .NET 10, Blazor interactive server, System.Text.Json, existing xUnit/WebApplicationFactory packages, Playwright MCP.
+
+**Spec:** Ticket #1, Approved Spec comment and the agreed scope in this conversation (small change; no separate design document).
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- Optional calendar day only, no time: API format `YYYY-MM-DD`.
+- Overdue means not done and due date strictly before today in UTC; no date means never overdue.
+- POST accepts optional `dueDate`; existing requests without it remain valid.
+- PATCH sets/changes `dueDate`, explicit null clears it, omission preserves it.
+- API responses include nullable `dueDate` and boolean `isOverdue`.
+- `GET /todos?overdue=true` filters to overdue items. Missing or false returns all.
+- The page has a checkbox labelled exactly `nur überfällige`, initially unchecked.
+- The page displays dates and marks overdue items with exactly `überfällig`.
+- No sorting, reminders, styling, new packages, or additional editing controls.
+- Validation remains in TodoStore and maps to HTTP 400 with an error JSON object.
+- All new UI elements used by tests have `data-testid` attributes.
+- Agent performs end-to-end tests in the running app and stops it afterward; screenshots go outside the repository.
+- Branch: `1_faelligkeitsdatum_todos`; base main; draft PR `WIP: 1: Fälligkeitsdatum für Todos`. Never merge or close the ticket.
+
+## Review Focus
+
+- Omitted versus null PATCH date: unrelated title/done updates preserve the date.
+- Calendar validation: reject timestamps, non-ISO formats and impossible dates without mutating data.
+- Completed items and UTC today: neither is overdue, including under filtering.
+- Status freshness: updates and later reads recompute the status; no stored overdue flag.
+- Browser interaction: checkbox updates the list after the Blazor circuit connects and restores all items when unchecked.
+
+## Task 1: Store dates and overdue rules
+
+**Files:** Modify `src/DemoTodo/TodoStore.cs`, `tests/DemoTodo.Tests/TodoStoreTests.cs`.
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- Consumes: existing TodoStore Add/Get/Update/List operations and request record constructors.
+- Produces: `Todo(int Id, string Title, bool Done, DateOnly? DueDate = null)` with computed `bool IsOverdue`; `NewTodo(string? Title, string? DueDate = null)`; TodoPatch with optional init `string? DueDate` and a JSON-ignored presence flag; `IReadOnlyList<Todo> List(bool overdueOnly = false)`.
+
+- [x] Write store tests for optional dates, valid leap day, yesterday/today/tomorrow, done and undated items, set/change/clear/preserve on PATCH, filtering and invalid dates (empty, whitespace, timestamp, locale date, impossible day).
+- [x] Run `dotnet test --filter FullyQualifiedName~TodoStoreTests`; confirm failure before production changes.
+- [x] Implement exact invariant date validation in TodoStore with ValidationException, preserving existing title validation and locks. Compute IsOverdue on access from DateTime.UtcNow; do not persist it. Parse a PATCH date before mutating state.
+- [x] Run the store tests; expect all passing. Commit source, tests and task progress.
+
+## Task 2: API contract and filter
+
+**Files:** Modify `src/DemoTodo/Program.cs`, `tests/DemoTodo.Tests/TodoApiTests.cs`.
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- Consumes: Task 1 records and `TodoStore.List(bool overdueOnly = false)`.
+- Produces: date/status JSON fields on POST/GET/list/PATCH; optional boolean query parameter `overdue` on GET /todos.
+
+- [x] First add HTTP tests using raw JSON shapes for POST dates and missing/null, GET date/status, PATCH omitted/null/set/change and done transitions, invalid strings/types on POST/PATCH, and true/false/absent filters. Update the old exact JSON expectation for the two new response fields.
+- [x] Run `dotnet test --filter FullyQualifiedName~TodoApiTests`; verify the new filtering test fails before changing the route.
+- [x] Bind nullable boolean overdue on the existing list route and call `store.List(overdue == true)`; keep the existing error mapping and other routes.
+- [x] Run `dotnet test`; expect all passing. Commit source, tests and task progress.
+
+## Task 3: List display and interactive filtering
+
+**Files:** Modify `src/DemoTodo/Components/Pages/Home.razor`; create `tests/DemoTodo.Tests/TodoPageTests.cs`.
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- Consumes: Task 1 Todo dates/status and filtered Store.List; page continues to use Store directly.
+- Produces: checkbox `data-testid="overdue-filter"` labelled `nur überfällige`, ISO date `data-testid="todo-due-date"`, visible `überfällig` marker `data-testid="todo-overdue"`; preserve existing list/item/title test ids.
+
+- [x] Write prerendered page tests for the checkbox, ISO date, overdue word only on open past-due rows, and preservation of done title markers and undated items. Decode HTML when asserting German copy.
+- [x] Run `dotnet test --filter FullyQualifiedName~TodoPageTests`; expect failures on the missing controls/markers.
+- [x] Add a native checkbox bound to a bool, foreach over Store.List(bool), ISO dates and the text marker; no CSS changes or timer.
+- [x] Run `dotnet test`; expect all passing. Commit source, tests and task progress.
+
+## Task 4: Verification, review and delivery
+
+- [x] Run `dotnet test` and `git diff --check` on the final branch.
+- [x] Start the app with `dotnet run --project src/DemoTodo --urls http://localhost:3000`; wait for GET /health.
+- [x] Seed yesterday, today, tomorrow, undated and completed past-date items through the API. Verify API filtering and the rendered dates/overdue labels with Playwright; wait for the Blazor circuit, check/uncheck `nur überfällige`, verify only the overdue row/all rows, and test the empty filtered state after marking the last overdue item done and reloading.
+- [x] Save screenshots outside the repo and stop the app. Record exact observations and any limitations in the implementation summary.
+- [x] Request a fresh whole-branch review per the review skill; address substantiated findings and recheck affected behavior.
+- [x] Commit the finished plan progress, push the branch, open the draft PR with the implementation summary and ticket reference.
+- [x] Read the cost include, post Implementation Summary and Cost Summary to ticket #1, then move its label from in-progress to review. Leave acceptance and merge to the human.
+
+## Delivery evidence
+
+- `dotnet test`: 46 passed, 0 failed; `git diff --check`: clean.
+- Playwright: 5 initial rows, 4 dates, 1 overdue marker on 2026-10-15 UTC; overdue-only filter on/off, API filtering and empty result after completion passed.
+- Screenshots outside the repo: `/tmp/ticket-1-all-todos.png`, `/tmp/ticket-1-only-overdue.png`, `/tmp/ticket-1-empty-overdue.png`. App stopped afterward.
+- Independent whole-branch review: no findings.
+- Draft PR: http://gitea:3000/adw/demo-todo/pulls/2. Ticket #1 has implementation and cost summaries and is in review.
+- Execution decision: the legacy exact JSON expectation was updated in task 1 rather than task 2 to keep the intermediate suite green; no product impact, only test sequencing.
